meta {
  name: List Aging Audits
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/management-dashboard/alerts/aging-audits?range=ytd
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  range: ytd
  ~page: 1
  ~pageSize: 50
  ~producerIds:
  ~leadSourceIds: {{mailerLeadSourceId}}
  ~policyTypes: Auto
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{managementDashboardToken}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("the total is the card's number", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().total).to.equal(bru.getVar("managementAgingAudits"));
  });

  test("every row is past the SLA and not Pass", function () {
    for (const row of res.getBody().items) {
      expect(row.auditStatus).to.not.equal("Pass");
      expect(row.businessDaysOpen).to.be.above(5);
      expect(row.soldDate).to.be.a("string");
    }
  });

  test("oldest sale first", function () {
    const dates = res.getBody().items.map((row) => Date.parse(row.soldDate));
    for (let i = 1; i < dates.length; i++) {
      expect(dates[i - 1]).to.be.at.most(dates[i]);
    }
  });
}

docs {
  # GET /management-dashboard/alerts/aging-audits — the Aging Audits drawer (PAC-139)

  One row per **deal** (never per audit item), oldest sale first. "You have
  five business days once a deal is sold to complete the audit. Any deal that
  is not completed by that time, that's aging" (David, 22 Sep 00:25:26).

  - **Module / permission / scope / filter / paging:** as `List Stalled Leads`.
  - **`total`** equals the card's `agingAudits` under the same query.
  - The clock is **business days from the sold date**: weekends and the eleven
    US federal holidays (observed days) are skipped, on the Chicago calendar.
    A deal sold on a Friday has had one business day by Monday.
  - **Open** means `auditStatus` is anything but `Pass` — Not Submitted,
    Pending and Fail all count. A deal with no audit record is not aging.

  The web opens each row on the household (`/clients/:householdId`) until the
  Deal Audit page ships (PAC-106); `dealAuditId` and `dealId` are here for it.

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  {
    "period": { "key": "ytd", "current": { "from": "2026-01-01", "to": "2026-09-23" }, "previous": { "from": "2025-01-01", "to": "2025-09-23" } },
    "page": 1, "pageSize": 50, "total": 3, "totalPages": 1,
    "items": [
      {
        "dealAuditId": "66f0…c3", "dealId": "66f0…d4", "householdId": "66f0…b2",
        "clientName": "Dana Whitfield", "producerId": "66f0…11", "producerName": "Pat Producer",
        "auditStatus": "Not Submitted", "openFailedCount": 1,
        "soldDate": "2026-09-11T05:00:00.000Z", "businessDaysOpen": 8
      }
    ]
  }
  ```

  ## Errors
  As `Get Alerts`.
}
